Z||000005||FieroJoe||03-09-2001||05:27 PM||||I watched a thing today on the news, all these 40 somethings saying that when a teen overhears a peer saying <I>anything</I> violent or something, that they need to report it immediatly and let the police or school administrators take care of it.  Lets look into a little teen logic right here.<P>1.  Hears from peer: "I want to kill Mrs. Gerard!  she is so stupid, I cant believe she gave me a C"<BR>2.  Says to peer: "Damn man, that sucks alot, there's always extra credit."<BR>3.  Teen does <B>not</B> think "Uh oh, I better go tell that hes going to bring a gun and kill the teacher"<P>...Or anything like that.  Point here is, kids joke around a hell of a lot, even the ones that are outcasts and picked on.  They just can't be taken seriously, because most of the time they arent.  Do you think that everytime I said "aww man you're dead!!" to someone, they actually thought I was going to murder them?  No, they didnt.<P>As with the case of the cali shooting where the kid told someone else that he was going to do it, the kid he told can't be blamed for what happend.  He was only being normal; not ratting on one of his peers for saying something that he's probably said before, but never acted on.<P>I blame the kid.  100% his fault.  Not guns, or having acess to guns.  I have access to guns.  All my friends do.  I shoot them a lot too, but at clay pigeons and pop cans.  No people.<P>I blame the kid for not being able to control his emotions and being a wuss.  Guns are for pussies that cant control themselves or deal with a problem in a mature manner.<P>Theres just my opinion.  Sorry for the rant.  I hope the kid gets life in prison, so he can be someone's "special friend" for the rest of his life.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||RNGCRSH||03-10-2001||03:29 AM||||FieroJoe, <P>I have to disagree. I dont want that kid to get life in prison. I want him to get the death penalty. Why should we pay $40,000 dollars a year of taxpayers' money to feed and clothe a murderer? I dont care if he was 14 y.o. or 10 y.o. All murders reguardless should be punished with the big sleep!<P>I do agree with every thing else. the kid was a F*&^ing coward, he didn't have the balls to stand up to his peers so he used a gun and a sneak attack.<P>And for his parents, How in the hell could the not know what was going on. Sometimes I swear mine have eyes in the back of thier heads with radar tracking. I'm 30 years old and live 400 miles away from them and they still somehow know when I'm up to no good. I would have never even gotten close to doing anything like this, my parent would have beat the crap out of me if I even made the threat of this kind of violence. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||GT Bastard||03-10-2001||08:28 AM||||I feel the same way about repeat rapists and other hard-core criminals.  They should simply be killed.  The world is already steadily becoming overpopulated.  We could take all the money we saved from killing them and help people who deserve it, or maybe a tax cut.  I think we should be less tolerant with people who inflict serious harm to others.  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||DaRkLoRD||03-10-2001||09:53 PM||||Right on RNGCRSH & GTB.. there are many debates about this every so often in my political science class. I tend to stay quiet because there are a lot more people who disagree with my viewpoint (same as yours, in this situation) than agree with me.<P>Not to get into details, but I was treated very badly in high school.. not many people were below me in social status. Because I kept it all inside and never stood up to anyone who was giving me sh*t, I'm kinda messed up now.. but I never considered taking a gun to school to shoot people.. nah, I always favored hijacking an F16 and shooting some nice missiles at my school..*  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>Oh well..<P>(*This was from a Calvin & Hobbes comic)<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||4
Z||000009||Will||03-10-2001||11:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by GT Bastard:<BR><B>I feel the same way about repeat rapists and other hard-core criminals.  They should simply be killed.  The world is already steadily becoming overpopulated.  We could take all the money we saved from killing them and help people who deserve it, or maybe a tax cut.  I think we should be less tolerant with people who inflict serious harm to others.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I've heard that with all the appeals, death row time, and motions for this, that, or the other thing, it's actually more expensive to put someone to death than to keep them in prison for life.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Eric||03-11-2001||12:16 AM||||For me, shooting a gun is no different than throwing a ball.  I don't get any more satisfaction from shooting a gun than I would otherwise get from playing catch.  That IS a primal satisfaction or urge to harm or inflict damage on someone else.  Too many people associate guns with death and murder.  As for me, I've been around guns for most of my life, and I have to say, the more comfortable I am with firing and handling firearms, the more I respect them.  If you were to ask someone who has never shot, held, or been around a gun before, to handle a firearm, this primal instict makes itself very very apparent.  Either the person will recoil at the sight of it or they'll be deeply intrigued.  And when you've proved your point, you'll practically have to pry the gun out of their hands.  I believe the combination of a lack of respect for firearms, a lack of respect for human life, and that very glint I described earlier of a sexual, Fruedian urge to kill when handling a gun can be a disasterous and leathal combination.  If you feel special or powerfull when you hold, carry, or fire a gun, for God's sake, don't have anything to do with them.  For the rest of us, enjoy you guns  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||Galen||03-11-2001||01:31 AM||||Hell yeah.. I just gotta add mine to this. <P>Big ears, skinny, funny lookin, goofey, all of that is me. I never let it bother me, I just let go as "Their dumba&&'s and I got better sh!t to do". Suprised they aint tried to make the 'violent' games and music back into this. I listen to violent music a good bit, it helps me relax, makes me feel at ease. I play violent games, gives me an outlet to shoot the hell out of my friends. Am I a violent person becuz of this? not really, Has my playin these violent games, listening to this violent music, and most of all getting picked on in school make me wanna go take out a bunch of school kids and their teachers? What did the teachers do? and the other students, I mean, if I was gonna go shoot someone at school becuz I was getting bullied or the such, it'd be the guy who was doing the bullying. Even then I wouldn't shoot him. As was said before, a gun is a sorry way out of a problem. Thats why evolution (hadda put that in here *g*) gave me two legs, feet, arms, & hands. Would I win in a fight? I doubt it, but atleast I could respect myself. And now I conclude my daily rant.||||reg||1
Z||000012||RNGCRSH||03-11-2001||11:58 AM||||Originally posted by Will:<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>I've heard that with all the appeals, death row time, and motions for this, that, or the other thing, it's actually more expensive to put someone to death than to keep them in prison for life.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>The only reason it does cost more right now to put someone on death row is because of our touchy feely gov. Evryone is so afraid we will put someone innocent to death that they get 15 appeals and it cost us much more.<BR>Give criminals 1 year and one appeal; if they are found guilty at the appeal then they get Death penalty within 48 hours. I also say if they are innocent and do get put to death, then God will take care of it. They will receive their rewards. This life on earth is nothing compared to what God makes available<P>We need swift and just punishment to be brought back to this country. It is a shame that we don’t have the compassion to end the life of a murderer who's mind is obviously so screwed that it can never be fixed.<P>The death penalty ensures we will not have criminals released for good behavior, getting out and murdering again.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000013||filthyscarecrow||03-11-2001||08:12 PM||||i know everyone who likes guns will disagree with me on this, or try to argue about it, but psychologists have done studies that prove that guns actually make people more aggressive. the mere presence of it affects them. not having to hold it, not even seeing it. as long as they know a gun is present, people tend to be more aggressive. i personally have a problem with them. i see no social good coming from an instrument whose sole reason for existing is to kill something or someone. obviously, we can't get rid of them though, as too many people will still be able to get a hold of them, but something should be done. why do handguns exist? to kill people, period. they are here to kill people. does that sound retarded and uncivilized to anyone else? why do we still even make handguns? <BR>  as for these shootings, i think the administration is to blame. teachers see students being bullied and picked on constantly yet do nothing. the school administration, when confronted with such a situation, does very little. if the bully is reported, they are told not to do it anymore. do they REALLY think that a slap on the wrist will stop someone from ruining someone else's life? we let these morons TEACH kids. why?! if i were a teacher and saw a student picking on another student, i would turn the tables on them. turn the rest of the class against them so that they know how it feels to have their life taken away. <BR>  i think these school shootings are 100% preventable if the administration at schools would open their F***ing eyes. going to school should be boring and tedious, not miserable and horrifying. i'm surprised my high school has never had one. i'm glad i'm outta there, but the way that place was run makes me wonder whether school officials are even human. i think the school officials should be held responsible too for not solving the problem when it first began...||||reg||1
