Z||000021||Galen||03-13-2001||04:11 PM||||thats wrong? yes the state makes mistakes, but I dont really think there is any arguement about school shootings, and who did em. or let me think, oh yes.. the kid had the gun in his hands, he pulled the trigger, the bullet came out of the gun while he was holding the gun and after he pulled the trigger, and that bullet hit someone in the head and killed them. But no, he's not guilty of murder, cuz it could have been someone else. but all the 'victoms' who didn't die say it was him, but how are we to know they arn't all telling a lie? maybe its a conspircy agaist the kid? Maybe the students didn't like em, and got together with the teachers to get the kid put to death? Or maybe its the FBI? CIA? or even the IRS? Did his parents pay their taxes on time? Yes courts do make mistakes, yes people lie. But its very unlikely, though as I said before not completely impossible, that he isn't guilty.||||reg||1
Z||000022||DaRkLoRD||03-13-2001||04:37 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ray b:<BR><B>we need one age law to be set for adult rights anyway be it 18 0r 21 or new # it must be same for all not diffrent in each state rules about each thing like now for crime drinking vote contract wed sex or draft ect. <BR>pick one age not to be changed for all laws.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>government shouldn't tell me when I can and cannot get married, have sex, drink, etc... it's none of their business. They can set limits on who can buy alcohol, but charging a 18 y/o (or 20 in the usa.. hehehe) for drinking "under age" is total BS. as for drafting/conscription.... no way in hell I'd fight for my country if they just told me to. I'm not willing to die for them. I'd defend my home if I needed to, but if Canada ever got involved in some crap like the vietnam war was, I'd tell my government what to go do with themselves. I have many friends in the military, and after seeing their behaviour now as opposed to before (joined fresh out of high school) they've changed a lot. their thinking is all oriented around conflict and orders.. and junk about protecting their country's freedom. Honestly, who's gonna take it away?? the USA could crush every other country on the planet..<P>------------------<BR>   <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>   <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A><p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 03-13-2001).]||||reg||8
